# Engineering Playbook (agent contract)

Canonical detail: `docs/ENGINEERING-PLAYBOOK.md`. Append **Lessons Learned** there after each work block.

## Mission

Leave the codebase more reliable, maintainable, fast, accessible, documented, and tested.

## Non-negotiables

- Privacy first; local-first when practical; never fabricate data.
- Honest loading states; progressive enhancement; shared design system.
- Simplicity over cleverness; smallest correct fix first.
- **Never commit or push unless the owner explicitly asks.**

## Workflow (every block)

Investigate → root cause → fix → architecture only if justified → tests → UX /
a11y / perf review → similar-defect sweep → docs → final report.

Operate through: Senior, UX, Performance, Accessibility, QA, Reliability,
Security, Documentation.

## Quality gates before claiming done

Root cause named · regression covered · relevant tests pass · no new console
errors · desktop/mobile considered · a11y + perf reviewed · docs updated.

## Architecture / UX / perf

Prefer progressive rendering, independent modules, graceful degradation.
Render shell immediately; no blocking on all providers; avoid duplicate
requests and layout thrash. Fail gracefully — never appear frozen.

## Reliability pattern

One defect ⇒ search the codebase for the same pattern (e.g. `[hidden]` vs
`display:flex`, progressive mounts that refetch, premature settle).

## Final report

Objective, root causes, improvements, tests, risks, recommendations, session
start/end if observable, runtime or **unavailable**.

## Dirty tree

Do not stage unrelated noise (`data/*`, generated status/debug, importer
desktop, local audit PDF scripts) unless the owner requests it.
